    "site_desc": "Corn field on Bouldin Island in the Sacramento San Joaquin Delta.  This site has deep peat that was drained for farming. Over the past 100 years there has been excessive subsidence of the peat in the Delta region. The corn is usually harvested for silage cattle feed.\nCorn was planted in the field 2017-2023. Sorghum was planted in the field 2024.",
